κάλαμος, -ου, ὁ 
[in LXX chiefly for קָנֶה, Isa.42.3, Ezk.40.3 ff., al. ;] 
a reed: Mat.11.7; 12.20" (LXX) Luk.7.24 hence, accusative, to its various uses, 
__(a) a reed-pipe, flute; 
__(b) a reed-staff, staff (cf. 2Ki.18.21, ῥάβδος καλαμίνη): Mat.27.29-30, 48, Mrk.15.19, 36; 
__(with) a measuring reed or rod (Ez, l.with): Rev.11.1; 21.15-16; 
__(d) a writing reed, a pen: 3Jn.13 (cf. Milligan, NTD, 9, 7).†
(AS)
